WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
POET: partial oral versus IV antibiotics for endocarditis.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Primary outcome with continued IV treatment: 12.1%.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
After switching to oral: 9.0%. Noninferior.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The noninferiority margin was 10 percentage points, and the whole confidence interval stayed inside it.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Median hospital stay after randomization: 3 days on oral vs 19 on IV.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Primary composite outcome: 12.1% IV vs 9.0% oral.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
By component: deaths 6.5% vs 3.5%; surgery, embolism, and relapse were the same in both arms.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Difference 3.1 points (95% CI -3.4 to 9.6). Per-protocol and sensitivity analyses also cleared the -10 margin.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Hospital stay: 19 days vs 3 days (not a prespecified outcome).

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
In stable patients, switching to oral antibiotics was noninferior to continuing IV.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
NEJM 2019. Scroll down for the full breakdown.
